fact WorkItem(id: "WI-1113", description: some(value: "anthill-todo backend, INCREMENT 1 of WI-437: STORE-FACTORY SUBSTRATE. Design: rustland/anthill-todo/docs/design/backend-github-coordination.md, §14 row 1 (with §3 and §8.2). Ships no user-visible change -- it is the seam every later increment hangs on. FIRST, AMEND THE DOC. §3 specifies `fact StoreBackend(kind: BackendKind)` in project.anthill as the configuration channel; it was written before WI-830, which landed `fact ExtentBinding(store:, role:, covers:)` in that same file doing that same job, plus role and coverage. Adding StoreBackend beside it gives one datum two writable homes -- the failure §7 is shaped to avoid. Reconcile: BackendKind's config rides `ExtentBinding.store` as an applied term (a `GithubCoordinatedStore(repo:, root:, project:, access:)` slots exactly where `IndexedFileStore(root:, convention:)` sits today), and decide what remains of §8.2's `open_store` existential now that the host already maps a declared store term to a compiled-in backend. Land the amendment as its own commit BEFORE any code, and fix the stale citation while there: §8.2's bare spec-op call is at main.anthill:3184, not :2837. THEN THE CODE. (a) Drop the vestigial `store: FileStore` parameter from `main`/`dispatch` and every `cmd_*`, with its `Modify[store]` effect -- VERIFIED vestigial: no body in main.anthill calls persist/retract/flush on it, and it is passed at 16 sites. This is the true prerequisite: a backend cannot be swapped while a concrete FileStore sits in main's type. Pure deletion. (b) Move `stamp_format(s, current_store_format())` at main.anthill:3184 to the dotted `WorkItemStore.stamp_format(...)` form -- the last of 44 spec-op sites still written bare, and per WI-402 a bare call to a body-less spec operation does not resolve through an existentially-typed receiver. (c) Whatever open_store reduces to under the amended design. Absent declaration -> today's behavior (WI-830's default_binding)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-08-16T16:48:11Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-1113", name: "wi437")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-1113", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-08-16, commits e6141d27 (doc amendment), d390628c (the deletion), 963284b8 (the open_store finding), e6a88064 (renumber), 072a8be1 (merge). Pushed as 12a43d04..072a8be1.\n\nTHE DOC AMENDMENT, three drifts. (1) §3's `fact StoreBackend(kind: BackendKind)` was overtaken by WI-830's `fact ExtentBinding(store:, role:, covers:)` in the same project.anthill -- same job plus role and coverage -- so StoreBackend is gone and layout is named by the store term in the extent binding. (2) The forge is now a PARAMETER, not a variant: the draft's `GithubCoordinated(repo:, root:, project:, access:)` and `fact GithubIssue` would have made GitLab or Gitea a new CONFIG variant, while §8.3 was already arguing GitHub is one implementation of a five-point contract. Now `fact Coordination(forge: GithubForge(...), access:)` on the same term-names-a-thing-to-build precedent as ExtentBinding.store, the link fact is forge-neutral `MirrorEntry(workitem:, entry:)`, and the carrier's operations are named neutrally (create_entry / recent_entries / entries_titled / entry_comments / add_to_board). (3) The state-dir layout is NOT `FileConvention::StateDirs` on IndexedFileStore -- that grafts one store's semantics onto another, and IndexedFileStore's fields say why (inner: FileStore, source_map: HashMap<RuleId,(PathBuf,Span)>, pending_span_retracts: \"flush drops the range from the file\"), all of it for MANY FACTS SHARE A FILE, ADDRESSED BY BYTE OFFSET. File-per-item is the opposite. It is `ItemPerFileStore`, a sibling implementation of the six-method Store trait that does not implement IndexedStore. New §5.2 carries the argument; FileConvention is untouched.\n\nAlso added: §14.1, the SELF-HOSTING CONSTRAINT, which is why the sibling-store shape is REQUIRED and not merely tidier -- anthill-todo is the tool tracking these increments, so a convention INSIDE IndexedFileStore would have made every increment surgery on the store the tracker was running on. The two stores coexist; this repo stays on IndexedFileStore through increment 5; the backend lands before any project declares it, since the host hard-refuses a store it lacks.\n\nTHE CODE. `store: FileStore` deleted from main/dispatch and all twelve mutating cmd_* -- 14 parameter declarations, 13 call sites, two Modify[store] rows, and NOT ONE BODY that read it. A concrete backend in main's type is exactly what makes a backend unswappable. Host drops the matching argument to call_with_requirements. The one bare spec-op call site is now `WorkItemStore.stamp_format(...)` like the other 43, and the member import of the spec's fifteen operations is deleted (no bare call site left to use it). Three stale signature docs fixed: anthill-stl/src/runner.rs, docs/design/operation-call-model.md, and §8.2 itself.\n\nWHAT SELECTION DID NOT NEED. The doc framed `open_store` as the mechanism that picks a backend. It is not: `sort Main` already declares `sort State = ?` with `requires WorkItemStore[State]`, every cmd_* takes Cell[State], and the host discharges the requirement with a dictionary. With the FileStore parameter gone the bundle is fully backend-abstract WITHOUT open_store. What remains coupled is narrower -- main.rs hand-builds the impl's state value, interning `anthill.todo.store.FileBasedWorkitemStore.wis` and its field names.\n\nOPEN_STORE DID NOT LAND, and it was measured rather than assumed. All three spellings were written, built and run: `-> C ensures WorkItemStore[C]` gives \"expected WorkItemStore, got WIS\"; `-> C ensures WorkItemStore[State = C]` gives \"unresolved name 'C'\" (the NAMED form is not detected as an existential at all, only the first-positional one); and `FileBasedWorkitemStore.wis(...)` from namespace scope gives \"unknown functor\", which decides the shape on its own -- a namespace-level factory cannot construct an impl's state, so it would have to live inside one impl, where it can no longer select between impls. WI-402's existential needs a CARRIER slot with the returned sort PROVIDING the spec (the delivered KVStore fixture's shape); WorkItemStore's only parameter IS State and satisfaction is `fact WorkItemStore[State = WIS]`. So the factory needs the spec restructured around a carrier, which only pays for itself at a second impl. Moved to WI-1114 with the measurement on that ticket and in new §8.2.1.\n\nTWO CLAIMS I MADE AND THEN MEASURED FALSE, corrected at their sites rather than dropped: (a) deleting the member import does NOT make the bare spelling unrepresentable -- with it gone, a bare `stamp_format(s, ...)` still LOADS and RUNS correctly, because the operation is in scope through `requires WorkItemStore[State]`; restored it, rebuilt, ran migrate, watched it stamp the file. It is a dead-import cleanup, not a guard. (b) The dotted call site has NO control today: migrate_stamps_pre_versioning_project passes with either spelling. The test that would fail on the bare form arrives with WI-1114's second store. Both are stated at their sites.\n\nREVIEW: /code-review at high, six findings, all six fixed (dead member import; a stale main.rs comment claiming command bodies still went through store: FileStore; an off-by-one \"thirteen\" cmd_* when it is twelve; the missing control statement; a §3.3 gap where a project declaring Coordination and NO binding escaped the layout check, since an absent binding DEFAULTS to single-file, so the check must read the EFFECTIVE binding; and a misattached `retreat` gloss in §8.3).\n\nDRIVEN, NOT MERELY LOADED: add / claim / feedback / tag / untag / deliver / delete round-trip on a fresh fixture, plus migrate on a stamp-stripped project asserting `fact StoreFormat(version: 1)` reaches disk. Self-hosting gate after every rebuild: the live tracker still answers status / list / show.\n\nAN ID COLLISION HAPPENED, and it is worth recording as evidence for this epic. These six increments were filed as WI-1108..WI-1113 when the local max was WI-1107; origin/main had meanwhile allocated WI-1108..WI-1112 for unrelated typing, codegen and perf work. Caught on the fetch before push -- the only place it CAN be caught today -- and resolved by renumbering these six to WI-1113..WI-1118 (descending, so no shift landed on a live id). The merge conflict underneath was a pure union, both sides appending to one file, carrying no disagreement. That is §1.1 and §1.2 happening to the tickets FOR §1.1 and §1.2: the layout change removes the first, increment 4's stake-by-creation removes the second.\n\nSUITE: full workspace, 35 binaries, 4920 passed, 0 failed, 11 ignored, exit 0, on the MERGED tree.", at: "2026-08-16T16:48:06Z")
